'''Michael Frass''' (born 1954) is an Austrian medicine specialist for [[internal medicine]] and professor at the [[Medical University of Vienna]] (MUW). He is known for his work on [[homeopathy]].

== Biography ==
He is First Chairman of the ''Scientific Society for Homeopathy'' (WissHom),<ref name="WissHom">{{cite web |title=Scientific Society for Homeopathy! |url=https://www.wisshom.de/ |website=wisshom.de |access-date=20 May 2021}}</ref> founded in 2010, president of the ''Umbrella organization of Austrian Doctors for Holistic Medicine'',<ref name="Dachverband">{{cite web |title=Österreichischer Dachverband für ärztliche Ganzheitsmedizin |url=https://www.ganzheitsmed.at/ |website=ganzheitsmed.at |access-date=20 May 2021 |language=de}}</ref> since 2002 and since 1994 Vicepresident of the ''Doctors Association for Classical Homeopathy''.<ref name="Ärtzeges">{{cite web |title=Ärztegesellschaft für klassische Homöopathie |url=http://www.aekh.at/ |website=aekh.at |access-date=20 May 2021 |language=de}}</ref>

== Homoeopathic research ==
A major interest of Frass is [[homeopathy]]. He has published several papers on this subject.

=== Article in ''the Oncologist'' ===
In 2020 Frass was the corresponding author of an article<ref>{{cite journal|journal=The Oncologist|title=Homeopathic Treatment as an Add-On Therapy May Improve Quality of Life and Prolong Survival in Patients with Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer: A Prospective, Randomized, Placebo-Controlled, Double-Blind, Three-Arm, Multicenter Study|volume=25|issue=12|pages=e1930–e1955|issn=1083-7159|pmc=8108047|pmid=33010094|date=2020-12-01|language=English|doi=10.1002/onco.13548 |last1=Frass |first1=Michael |last2=Lechleitner |first2=Peter |last3=Gründling |first3=Christa |last4=Pirker |first4=Claudia |last5=Grasmuk-Siegl |first5=Erwin |last6=Domayer |first6=Julian |last7=Hochmair |first7=Maximilian |last8=Gaertner |first8=Katharina |last9=Duscheck |first9=Cornelia |last10=Muchitsch |first10=Ilse |last11=Marosi |first11=Christine |last12=Schumacher |first12=Michael |last13=Zöchbauer-Müller |first13=Sabine |last14=Manchanda |first14=Raj K. |last15=Schrott |first15=Andrea |last16=Burghuber |first16=Otto }}{{Retracted|doi=10.1093/oncolo/oyaf364|pmid=41277743|https://retractionwatch.com/2024/09/26/homeopathy-for-cancer-paper-extensively-corrected-after-watchdog-agency-requested-retraction/ ''Retraction Watch''|intentional=yes}}</ref> in the medical journal ''The Oncologist'' which concluded that additional homoeopathic treatment improves [[Quality of life (healthcare)|quality of life]] and [[Survival rate|survival rates]] in patients with [[Non-small-cell lung cancer|non‐small cell lung cancer]] (NSCLC). The results of the article were discussed outside of academic circles, for example in the [[Wiener Zeitung]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Komplementärmedizin - Studie sieht verbesserte Lebensqualität bei Lungenkrebs|url=https://www.wienerzeitung.at/nachrichten/wissen/mensch/2098072-Studie-zeigt-Erfolg-bei-Lungenkrebs.html|access-date=2022-11-20|last=Alexandra Grass|date=26 March 2021|language=de|pages=|quote=}}</ref> After criticism (for example from the Informationsnetzwerk Homöopathie<ref>{{cite web|title=Verbesserungen beim Überleben von Lungenkrebspatienten mit homöopathischer Komplementärbehandlung (Frass et al. 2020) – Pressemitteilung des INH (31.10. / 03.11.2022)|periodical=Informationsnetzwerk Homöopathie|publisher=|url=https://netzwerk-homoeopathie.info/frass-et-al-2020-pressemitteilung-inh-mit-update-2022-11-03/|format=|access-date=2022-11-20|last=INH-Team|date=2022-11-03|language=de-DE|pages=|quote=}}</ref>), the ''Austrian Agency for Scientific Integrity'' (Österreichische Agentur für wissenschaftliche Integrität) concluded that the article contains [[Scientific misconduct|data manipulation and forgery]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Homöopathie: Wie gehabt, eine neue Mogelei|periodical=|publisher=[[Der Standard]]|url=https://www.derstandard.at/story/2000140529797/homoeopathie-wie-gehabt-eine-neue-mogelei|format=|access-date=2022-11-20|last=Christian Kreil|date=2022-11-08|language=de-AT|pages=|quote=}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Homöopathie bei Krebspatienten: Fast zu schön, um wahr zu sein|periodical=|publisher=Profil|url=https://www.profil.at/wissenschaft/homoeopathie-bei-krebspatienten-fast-zu-schoen-um-wahr-zu-sein/402198219|format=|access-date=2022-11-20|last=Alwin Schoenberger|date=2022-10-28|language=de|pages=|quote=}}</ref> ''The Oncologist'' released an [[expression of concern]] in 2022<ref>{{Cite journal|title=Expression of Concern: Homeopathic Treatment as an Add-On Therapy May Improve Quality of Life and Prolong Survival in Patients with Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer: A Prospective, Randomized, Placebo-Controlled, Double-Blind, Three-Arm, Multicenter Study|url=https://academic.oup.com/oncolo/article/27/12/e985/6782256|journal=The Oncologist|date=2022-12-09|issn=1083-7159|pmc=9732219|pmid=36314553|pages=e985–e985|volume=27|issue=12|doi=10.1093/oncolo/oyac221|language=en}}</ref> and [[Retraction in academic publishing|retracted]] the article in November 2025.<ref>{{Cite journal|title=Retraction of: Homeopathic Treatment as an Add-On Therapy May Improve Quality of Life and Prolong Survival in Patients with Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer: A Prospective, Randomized, Placebo-Controlled, Double-Blind, Three-Arm, Multicenter Study|url=https://academic.oup.com/oncolo/article/doi/10.1093/oncolo/oyaf364/8340391|journal=The Oncologist|date=2025-11-11|issn=1083-7159|pmc=12641399|pmid=41277743|volume=30|issue=11|doi=10.1093/oncolo/oyaf364|language=en}}</ref>

