== Invention ==
Rapid assessment and management of respiratory structure and function are imperative in emergency intubation.<ref>{{cite journal | doi=10.1097/00000542-199112000-00021 | title=Management of the Difficult Adult Airway with Special Emphasis on Awake Tracheal Intubation | date=1991 | last1=Biebuyck | first1=Jullen F. | last2=Benumof | first2=Jonathan L. | journal=Anesthesiology | volume=75 | issue=6 | pages=1087–1110 | pmid=1824555 }}</ref> [[Endotracheal intubation]] remains the gold standard in airway maintenance. However, endotracheal intubation may be impossible due to difficult circumstances with respect to space and illumination or [[anatomy]] even for skilled physicians. Therefore, the need arises for an alternative. The [[Combitube]] was designed with this goal in mind.<ref>{{cite journal | doi=10.1080/10903120090941065 | title=S Uccessful P Rehospital a Irway M Anagement by Emt-D S U Sing the C Ombitube | date=2000 | last1=Ochs | first1=Mel | last2=Vilke | first2=Gary M. | last3=Chan | first3=Theodore C. | last4=Moats | first4=Thomas | last5=Buchanan | first5=Jean | journal=Prehospital Emergency Care | volume=4 | issue=4 | pages=333–337 | pmid=11045413 }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal | doi=10.1016/s0300-9572(01)00441-5 | title=Use of the esophageal tracheal combitube™ by basic emergency medical technicians | date=2002 | last1=Lefrançois | first1=Daniel P. | last2=Dufour | first2=Daniel G. | journal=Resuscitation | volume=52 | issue=1 | pages=77–83 | pmid=11801352 }}</ref><ref>Frass M, Salem MR, Vaida S, Hagberg CA. Esophageal-tracheal double-lumen airways: the Combitube and Easytube. Benumof and Hagberg's Airway Management, 3rd Edition, 2013, Publisher Saunders.</ref>

Frass is the inventor of the Combitube, a twin lumen device designed for use in emergency situations and difficult airways. He has published several papers on this topic.<ref name="Combitube-3">{{cite journal | doi=10.1097/00005373-198911000-00004 | title=Esophageal Tracheal Combitube, Endotracheal Airway, and Mask | date=1989 | last1=Frass | first1=Michael | last2=Rodler | first2=Suzanne | last3=Frenzer | first3=Reinhard | last4=Ilias | first4=Wilfried | last5=Leithner | first5=Christian | last6=Lackner | first6=Franz | journal=The Journal of Trauma: Injury, Infection, and Critical Care | volume=29 | issue=11 | pages=1476–1479 | pmid=2585558 }}</ref>

